
  Track C GPU appliance (read-only root, CUDA via rootless containers)

  Write and run your own CUDA code:
    cd ~/cuda                                   # persistent workspace
    cuda-dev nvcc -arch=sm_89 -o vec examples/vector_add.cu
    cuda-dev ./vec
    cuda-dev                                    # shell with nvcc, cuBLAS, cuRAND, cuFFT

  More CUDA libraries (needs internet):
    cuda-dev list                               # cuDNN, cuSOLVER, cuSPARSE, NCCL, NPP, ...
    cuda-dev install cudnn                      # into your toolkit, not the read-only system

  GPU status:      gpu-status  (live: gpu-watch, Ctrl-C quits; rerun benchmark: gpu-bench)

